int bc_debug_skip(bc_client_t *c);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Skips the currently stopped command without executing it and advances to
the next command.
The function sends a \f[CR]skip\f[R] command on \f[CR]CHAN_DEBUG\f[R]
(channel 4).
.PP
The skipped command is treated as if it returned exit status 0
(success).
No side effects from the command occur: no files are modified, no
processes are spawned, and no variable assignments take effect.
.PP
After skipping, the debugger stops at the next command (as if
\f[CR]bc_debug_step()\f[R] were called, but without executing the
current command).
A new break\-hit event is generated.
.PP
This is useful for:
.IP \(bu 2
Preventing destructive commands (e.g., \f[CR]rm \-rf\f[R]) from
executing during a debugging session.
.IP \(bu 2
Testing control flow by skipping over specific commands.
.IP \(bu 2
Bypassing commands that would hang or produce unwanted side effects.
.PP
This function should be called when the debugger is stopped at a
breakpoint.
Calling it when not stopped is a no\-op.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]c\f[R] \(em Pointer to an authenticated \f[CR]bc_client_t\f[R]
connection.
Must not be NULL.
